spans.s:
सम्-√ आप् P. -आप्नोति, to acquire or obtain completely, gain, AV.; MBh. &c.;
to accomplish, fulfil, ŚBr.; KātyŚr.;
to reach, AV. :
Caus. आपयति, to cause to gain or obtain completely, ŚBr.;
to bring to an end, finish, complete, conclude, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to put an end to, put to death, destroy (with or scil. अत्मानम् ‘one's self’), Āpast.; Kathās.; BhP. :
Desid. of Caus. -आपिपयिथति, to wish or try to accomplish, ŚBr. :
Desid. -इप्सति, to wish to obtain or reach or accomplish, wish for, desire, ib.

सम्-आ-√ पत् P. -पतति, to fly together towards, rush violently upon, attack, assail (acc.), MBh.; R. &c.;
to descend, alight, VarBṛS.;
to come together, be united sexually with (सह), MBh.;
to come to, attain, ib.

सम्-आ-√ पद् Ā. -पद्यते, to fall upon, attack, assail, MBh.;
to fall into any state or condition, attain to, undergo, incur, ib. &c.;
to undertake, begin, Kāraṇḍ.;
to take place, occur, appear, APrāt., Sch.:
Caus. -पदयति, to cause to come to pass, MW.;
to bring about, complete, accomplish, ib.;
to restore, ib.

सम्-आ-√ पॄ Pass. -पूर्यते, to become completely full, be quite filled, MBh. :
Caus. -पूरयति, to make quite full, fill out with (instr.), ŚBr.;
to draw or bend (a bow), R.

सम्-आ-√ प्लु Ā. -प्लवते, to immerse together, immerse in water, bathe, MBh.; Hariv.;
to overflow, inundate, overwhelm, MBh.;
to spring or rush upon (acc.), R.;
to come into violent collision with, MBh.
